# pdf-bookshelf/.dropboxignore
#
# Project-scoped rules. Everything workspace-wide (node_modules, logs, tmp,
# .env, .DS_Store) already comes from ../.dropboxignore — only put rules here
# that genuinely should NOT apply to every project, which is what that file
# says to do for `storage`.

# ---- The PDF corpus ----
# storage/ holds the purchased PDFs the app serves - ~800 of them once this is
# loaded with production-shaped data, and licensed content that has no business
# replicating into a personal Dropbox. The canonical copy lives on the server;
# this directory is a local convenience, rebuilt by restoring from there or by
# uploading through the dashboard.
#
# Also avoids Dropbox writing to files under an app that is actively streaming
# them, and the "(conflicted copy)" files that produces.
#
# Added while the directory held only two 1 MB test files, per the workspace
# convention of excluding a heavy directory BEFORE it fills up.
#
# NOTE: like .env, this is not regenerable by sync. Once applied the directory
# is removed from the cloud and from other devices, surviving only where a copy
# already exists.
storage
